# Supabase Edge Functions — Production Trial
#
# supabase login
# supabase link --project-ref tfpahfhrclojmbfvwasg
#
# Plaid (Production keys from Dashboard → Keys → Production):
# supabase secrets set PLAID_CLIENT_ID=...
# supabase secrets set PLAID_SECRET=...        # must be PRODUCTION secret, not sandbox
# supabase secrets set PLAID_ENV=production
# supabase secrets set ANDROID_PACKAGE_NAME=com.family.bankapp
#
# App ↔ Edge Function auth (REQUIRED — functions fail closed without this).
# Must match FamilyAppConfig.EDGE_FUNCTION_SECRET (≥16 characters):
# supabase secrets set FAMILY_APP_API_SECRET=...
#
# Run SQL migrations in order through 007 (007 locks PostgREST to service_role only).
#
# supabase functions deploy plaid-link-token
# supabase functions deploy plaid-exchange
# supabase functions deploy plaid-accounts-sync
# supabase functions deploy plaid-transactions-sync
# supabase functions deploy plaid-items-list
# supabase functions deploy plaid-item-remove
# supabase functions deploy plaid-status
#
# Compliance notes:
# - Plaid access tokens live in plaid_item_vault (service role only), never on the phone.
# - Plaid secret never in the app; only in Supabase secrets.
# - FAMILY_APP_API_SECRET is required on every Edge Function call (X-Family-Bank-Key).
# - anon/authenticated cannot read tables or execute RPCs; use plaid-status instead.
# - Supabase free tier includes Edge Functions (500k invocations/mo).
# - Complete Plaid application/company profile before Production.
# - Add a privacy policy URL in Plaid Dashboard before Production (family use still recommended).
